krdp 6.7.5: with NLA, don't re-check the Client Info PDU's credentials in onPostConnect.
NLA already verified them against the SAM file; FreeRDP 3.32 clients (krdc 26.08) don't
repeat them in the Info PDU, so the comparison rejected every logged-in user with
"PostConnect for peer failed". krdp master trusts NLA here when PAM isn't in use.

--- a/src/RdpConnection.cpp	2026-10-08 10:21:14.911496013 -0400
+++ b/src/RdpConnection.cpp	2026-10-08 10:21:14.911521661 -0400
@@ -542,6 +542,12 @@
             qCDebug(KRDP) << "PAM authentication succeeded for user" << username;
             return true;
         }
+    } else {
+        // NLA has already checked the user and password against the SAM file (createSamFile),
+        // and a client may leave them out of the Client Info PDU (FreeRDP 3.32 does), so the
+        // comparison below would reject a logged-in user. krdp master trusts NLA here too.
+        qCDebug(KRDP) << "User" << username << "authenticated by NLA";
+        return true;
     }
 
     const auto users = d->server->users();
